extends RefCounted
## Everyday knowledge of the age of towns, temples and early states: practices,
## customs, methods and arrangements from roughly 3800 to 1500 BC (game years
## about 180 to 600). The great questions of the age (writing, bronze, wheels,
## written law) take decades, and without these a people's research teams ran
## far ahead of their age. With them every research line keeps questions of
## its own age, so inquiry broadens what a society knows instead of reaching for
## far later work. These are knowledge only: no buildings, production lines,
## recipes or equipment. Their consequences are small bounded effects; none
## accelerate research itself. Each was checked against the whole catalog, and
## none repeats an existing question under another name.
##
## Each entry is adopted into the 0-600 design (tools/research/
## design_amendments_600.json, "adopt"), which sets its band, foundations and
## pace; its painting is a related subject's (data/research/effects, "art").
## The ordering day and chance below repeat the design's own values.

